<title>AUSTRALIA: Long Australian bond yields fall awaiting budget.</title>
<headline>Long Australian bond yields fall awaiting budget.</headline>
<text>
<p>-------------(Snapshot at 9.05 A.M./2305 GMT)------------------</p>
<p>FUTURES					  CASH YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS  (JUN) 93.99  (UNCH)	6.07    (UNCH)</p>
<p>3-YR T-BONDS  (JUN) 93.19  (UNCH)	6.76    (UNCH)</p>
<p>10-YR T-BONDS (JUN) 92.330 (+0.015)    7.64    (- 0.02)</p>
<p>AUD/USD 0.7798(PREV 0.7775) US 30-YR   6.89    (UNCH)</p>
<p>------------------------(May 13)-------------------------------</p>
<p>*Long-dated Australian bond yields edged to their lowest level since late February in early trading in the wake of a firmer bias in U.S. debt and ahead of the Federal budget.</p>
<p>*1997/98 budget to be handed down at 7.30 p.m. (0930 GMT).</p>
